# Frontend design

For **new** landing/promotional UI (skip if matching an existing design system):

- One first-viewport composition; brand as hero signal (brand test without nav).
- Expressive fonts (not Inter/Roboto/Arial/system). Atmosphere bg (not flat).
- Full-bleed hero; budget: brand + one headline + one line + CTAs + one dominant image. No overlays/chips/cards in hero.
- One job per section. Real imagery > abstract gradients. Motion 2–3 purposeful.
- Avoid AI-default looks: purple gradients, cream+serif+terracotta, broadsheet hairlines; also dark-mode/purple/glow/pill/emoji defaults unless the product already uses them.
- Mobile + desktop. Prefer existing React patterns in-repo; no default `useMemo`/`useCallback` unless the codebase does.
